ReelSmith Privacy Policy
Effective Nov 4, 2026
ReelSmith keeps your data on your own computer. It has no servers or user accounts of its own, collects no analytics, and never sells or shares your data with advertisers.
1. About this policy
This policy explains what information ReelSmith, a desktop application for creating and posting short videos, handles when you use it, including when you connect your TikTok account. It applies to the ReelSmith app and its optional phone companion. Each platform and service you connect has its own privacy policy, which applies to the data they hold.
2. Information ReelSmith collects
From TikTok, when you connect your account, ReelSmith requests only these permissions:
• Basic profile (user.info.basic): your TikTok user ID, display name and profile picture, used to show which account you're posting to.
• Posting (video.publish, video.upload): lets ReelSmith upload a video to your account when you press Post. With it, ReelSmith receives your account's posting options (such as allowed privacy settings and maximum video length) and the status of each post.
• Access tokens that TikTok issues so ReelSmith can act for you. ReelSmith never sees your TikTok password.
That you create or enter in ReelSmith:
• Topics, scripts, captions, hashtags, narration audio, images and finished videos.
• Voice recordings, if you record narration yourself.
• Settings, and the API keys you enter for the services ReelSmith uses.
ReelSmith does not collect your location, contacts, browsing history, or usage analytics, and it does not use cookies or trackers.
3. How it's used and where it goes
ReelSmith uses your information only to make the videos you ask for and post them where you choose. It is stored on your computer: access tokens and API keys in your operating system's secure credential store (such as Windows Credential Manager), and everything else in ReelSmith's folder on your computer.
